# A copy of a function into itself goes by the limit of copies in loops WITHOUT objects. The wider limit is for a copy that may let an object fall away; what a function hands to itself
# and gets from itself does not. `shift` copied three times into itself was 3.6 times its bytes and 7% MORE instructions (a reducer of lambda terms: +3.5% in all). `size` is small: it is copied.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK-NOT: frame 1
# CHECK: = CallDirect {{*}}function=f1
# RUN(SMALL): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# SMALL-LABEL: code f2:Body
# SMALL: frame 1 callee=f2
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: the source prints the same
